\fs36 \cf0 1. Objective\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The objective of this stage is to 
\f0\b adapt the CubiCasa-trained model to German architectural floor plans
\f1\b0 , which differ significantly in:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
drawing conventions,\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
symbol styles,\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
line thickness,\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
and overall layout density.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Rather than training a model from scratch, a 
\f0\b fine-tuning approach
\f1\b0  was adopted to transfer structural knowledge (walls, doors, windows) learned from CubiCasa to the German domain.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
